(HEART ANATOMY - STUDY NOTES \(sample document\)) Tj
T*
T*
(1. The four chambers) Tj
T*
(The heart has four chambers. The right atrium receives oxygen-poor blood) Tj
T*
(from the body through the superior and inferior vena cava. The right) Tj
T*
(ventricle pumps that blood to the lungs through the pulmonary valve.) Tj
T*
(The left atrium receives oxygen-rich blood from the lungs via the pulmonary) Tj
T*
(veins. The left ventricle pumps oxygen-rich blood into the aorta; it has the) Tj
T*
(thickest muscular wall because it must supply the entire body.) Tj
T*
T*
(2. The heart valves) Tj
T*
(Four valves ensure one-way blood flow. The tricuspid valve lies between the) Tj
T*
(right atrium and right ventricle. The mitral \(bicuspid\) valve lies between the) Tj
T*
(left atrium and left ventricle. The pulmonary valve guards the exit of the) Tj
T*
(right ventricle, and the aortic valve guards the exit of the left ventricle.) Tj
T*
(The closing of these valves produces the classic 'lub-dub' heart sounds.) Tj
T*
T*
(3. Path of blood through the heart) Tj
T*
(Body -> superior/inferior vena cava -> right atrium -> tricuspid valve ->) Tj
T*
(right ventricle -> pulmonary valve -> pulmonary arteries -> lungs ->) Tj
T*
(pulmonary veins -> left atrium -> mitral valve -> left ventricle ->) Tj
T*
(aortic valve -> aorta -> body.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
