(HEART ANATOMY - STUDY NOTES \(sample document\), page 2) Tj
T*
T*
(4. Pulmonary and systemic circulation) Tj
T*
(Pulmonary circulation carries blood between the heart and the lungs: the) Tj
T*
(right ventricle pumps oxygen-poor blood to the lungs, and the pulmonary) Tj
T*
(veins return oxygen-rich blood to the left atrium. Systemic circulation) Tj
T*
(carries blood between the heart and the rest of the body: the left) Tj
T*
(ventricle pumps oxygen-rich blood through the aorta, and the vena cavae) Tj
T*
(return oxygen-poor blood to the right atrium. The two circuits operate in) Tj
T*
(series, so blood passes through the heart once for every full body loop.) Tj
T*
T*
(5. The cardiac conduction system) Tj
T*
(The heart generates its own electrical rhythm. The sinoatrial \(SA\) node in) Tj
T*
(the right atrium is the natural pacemaker. It sends an impulse to the) Tj
T*
(atrioventricular \(AV\) node, which delays the signal slightly so the atria) Tj
T*
(can finish contracting. The impulse then travels down the Bundle of His,) Tj
T*
(through the left and right bundle branches, and finally spreads through the) Tj
T*
(Purkinje fibres, causing the ventricles to contract from the bottom up.) Tj
T*
T*
(6. Basic cardiovascular physiology) Tj
T*
(Cardiac output is the volume of blood pumped per minute and equals heart) Tj
T*
(rate multiplied by stroke volume. Blood pressure is roughly cardiac output) Tj
T*
(times peripheral resistance. Arteries carry blood away from the heart,) Tj
T*
(veins return blood to the heart, and capillaries are the thin vessels where) Tj
T*
(oxygen, carbon dioxide and nutrients are exchanged with tissues.) Tj
T*
ET
